Both files below include the http-client import and the per-call enrichment fetch you asked for. A few details on how I implemented it:

- **Fetch method:** the fetch uses `http-client.fetch`, which returns transport failures as values. A dead or slow metadata endpoint therefore cannot fail the node.
- **Output unchanged:** the response is read and discarded, so the `Digest` is the same with or without the fetch.
- **What "the input's text" is:** the inputs have no single text field, so I used the run date plus the selected entry titles. These are percent-encoded and capped at 1,000 characters.
- **Still pending:** the graph definition doesn't grant http-client yet, so this world may be rejected until the graph update you mentioned ships.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{selection, run-info, digest};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(selected: selection, info: run-info) -> digest;
}
```

